  "body": "> Replaces #348, which GitHub closed when a push landed after the fork left NeoTech's network. Main is now merged in; the one conflict was `commands/mod.rs`, where both sides are kept (#368's `tool_body` and this PR's `tool_import`). `tool_library` passes 12/12, the UI tool-editor tests 5/5 including `tool_editor_snapshot`, and clippy for app and ui is clean. You already checked export and import by hand on #348.\n\n## What changed\nA CamCraft-native tool library file (the native half of #300's triage):\n- **Export library…** on the Tool library page writes the document's tools as `{\"format\":\"camcraft-tools\",\"version\":1,\"units\":\"mm\",\"tools\":[{name, definition}]}` (`.camtools`). Each `definition` comes from the existing `project::tool_to_json` / `tool_from_json`, the same tool shape `.camproj` stores and MCP speaks, so there's no second field mapping. Tool numbers are not exported.\n- **Import library…** reads it back (a bare MCP-style `[{name, definition}]` array is accepted too) as **one undo step** (`ImportTools`).\n- The whole file is checked before anything lands. Bad JSON, a wrong format/version/units, a missing required field, a nameless tool, a name used twice, a reserved name (Stock, G54…), or a tool `Tool::is_sane` refuses each refuse the import by the tool's name, with nothing applied.\n- A name already in the document is never overwritten: an identical tool is skipped, and a different one arrives as `\"<name> (2)\"`. A library that is already fully present refuses with \"nothing to import\" rather than adding an empty undo step.\n\nVendor formats (Fusion `.json`, `.hsmlib`) are **not** included - that stays the owner's clean-room call, so this PR says `Refs #300` and the issue stays open.\n\nCode: `crates/app/src/tool_library.rs`, `crates/app/src/commands/tool_import.rs`, `crates/ui/src/state_tool_library.rs` (state.rs only gets a 2-line module include), about 20 lines in `pages.rs::tool_page`.\n\n## Readings\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_library`: 11 passed. tool_numbers, tool_law, tool_gate, mcp, commands_undo: all pass.\n- Quick gate (app + ui suites): green except the known ones - `probe_op::every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag` (red on main, #344 / PR #345) and the GPU headless tests (`headless_run_succeeds`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`; no graphics adapter here).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- **Snapshot:** `crates/ui/tests/snapshots/egui_tool_editor.png` was regenerated on **macOS** - the new buttons show behind the editor window, nothing else moved. Per #255 these goldens are platform-sensitive; it may need regenerating on the CI platform.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/tool_library.rs`)\n`export_then_import_roundtrips_exactly`, `bare_mcp_array_imports_too`, `empty_document_refuses_export`, `duplicate_identical_is_skipped_and_different_is_renamed_never_overwritten`, `library_already_in_document_refuses_with_nothing_applied`, `insane_tool_refuses_whole_file_by_name`, `missing_required_field_refuses_by_name`, `malformed_and_foreign_files_refuse_cleanly`, `name_twice_in_file_refuses`, `reserved_name_refuses_with_nothing_applied`, `import_is_one_undo_unit_and_redo_restores_it`\n\n## GUI check (why this stays a draft)\n1. Setup > Tools: add a few catalog tools; **Export library…** -> save `tools.camtools`.\n2. New document: **Import library…** that file; the tools appear, status line \"imported N tools\".\n3. Ctrl+Z removes them all; Ctrl+Y brings them back.\n4. Import into a document with a different tool under one of the same names: it arrives as `<name> (2)`.\n5. Import a damaged file: the Tool pane shows a refusal naming the tool.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/300-tool-library-io.md`.\n\nChangelog: The Tool library page exports the document's tools to a `.camtools` file and imports one back (one undo step; names already in the document are never overwritten, and a bad file is refused by tool name)\n\nRefs #300\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
